  "answer": "Implemented `paginate` in `pagination.mjs`. Key points:\n\n- **Validation**: throws `TypeError` for non-array `items`; throws `RangeError` for `page`/`pageSize` that aren't positive safe integers (using `Number.isSafeInteger`, which also rejects `NaN`, `Infinity`, floats, and non-numbers).\n- **1-based paging**: `start = (page - 1) * pageSize`, so page 1 returns the first `pageSize` elements.\n- **`totalPages`**: `Math.ceil(items.length / pageSize)` — empty input yields `0`.\n- **`nextPage`**: `page + 1` only when `page < totalPages`, otherwise `null`. This handles empty input, the last page, and out-of-range pages (which return empty `items` while preserving the real `totalPages`).\n- **No mutation**: uses `slice`, which returns a new array and doesn't touch the input or its elements.\n- Named export preserved.",
